From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keystone P550 Integration <keystone-p550@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sm: use the native OpenSBI 1.6 trap entry for enclaves

The VF2 monitor's copied trap.S targets an older OpenSBI trap-frame ABI and
locks a P550 hart when installed as mtvec. Keep mtvec on OpenSBI 1.6's native
_trap_handler, which owns the exact struct sbi_trap_context assembly ABI.
Dispatch to Keystone's C handler while the current hart is in enclave context;
the handler updates that same context with the enclave or restored host state.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [P550/OpenSBI 1.6 integration]
---
 lib/sbi/sbi_trap.c       | 12 ++++++++++++
 keystone-sm/src/thread.c |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/sbi/sbi_trap.c b/lib/sbi/sbi_trap.c
index 9b7e0b8..9cef840 100644
--- a/lib/sbi/sbi_trap.c
+++ b/lib/sbi/sbi_trap.c
@@ -25,0 +26,5 @@
+
+#ifdef BOARD_P550_TEST
+extern int cpu_is_enclave_context(void);
+extern void sbi_trap_handler_keystone_enclave(struct sbi_trap_context *tcntx);
+#endif
@@ -299,6 +304,13 @@ struct sbi_trap_context *sbi_trap_handler(struct sbi_trap_context *tcntx)
  */
 struct sbi_trap_context *sbi_trap_handler(struct sbi_trap_context *tcntx)
 {
+#ifdef BOARD_P550_TEST
+	if (cpu_is_enclave_context()) {
+		sbi_trap_handler_keystone_enclave(tcntx);
+		return tcntx;
+	}
+#endif
+
 	int rc = SBI_ENOTSUPP;
 	const char *msg = "trap handler failed";
 	struct sbi_scratch *scratch = sbi_scratch_thishart_ptr();
diff --git a/keystone-sm/src/thread.c b/keystone-sm/src/thread.c
index f83efca..ae69814 100644
--- a/keystone-sm/src/thread.c
+++ b/keystone-sm/src/thread.c
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 #include "thread.h"
 
 void switch_vector_enclave(void){
-  csr_write(mtvec, &trap_vector_enclave);
+  csr_write(mtvec, &_trap_handler);
 }
 
 void switch_vector_host(void){
